# License

ACZPropNav — proportional-navigation missile guidance for
**ACE COMBAT ZERO: THE BELKAN WAR** (Steam, Windows x64).

This file covers everything in this repository that was written for this
project. It does **not** cover the game, and it does **not** relicense one
vendored third-party script; both are called out below.

---

## 1. Copyright

    Copyright (c) 2025-2026 silicer

(`silicer` is the project's author handle; substitute the legal name here if it
ever differs, and keep the years accurate.)

## 2. No game data or game assets are distributed

This repository contains **no** part of ACE COMBAT ZERO: THE BELKAN WAR and no
derived asset: no executable, no `*.arc` archive, no `*.wpb`/`*.wpt` data file,
no texture, model, audio or text table, and no extracted dump of any of those.

What the documentation *does* contain is interoperability information obtained
by observation — RVAs/offsets, structure layouts, and small numeric values read
out of the shipping game's own data (e.g. "the vanilla `mis.wpb` record has
`scope = 1600`"). Those are facts needed to write a compatible mod; they are
not a redistribution of the game's assets. The mod is an unmodified install
add-on: it reads `ACZPropNav.ini` and patches its own process at runtime. It
never modifies `acz.exe`, `*.arc` files or save data.

ACE COMBAT ZERO: THE BELKAN WAR and all related marks are trademarks of their
respective owners (Bandai Namco Entertainment). This project is unofficial and
is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or supported by Bandai Namco.

## 3. NOTICE — third-party and original components

* `tools/arc/upstream/aczarc.py` — **vendored community script, not MIT.**
  It is the archive unpack/repack script published with the "ACZ Enhanced
  Gunplay" mod on moddb (`ACZ_Enhanced_Gunplay_Mod_A6.zip`,
  MD5 `bd226c83426b8e1c856737aae3a5d25b`,
  <https://www.moddb.com/games/ace-combat-zero-the-belkan-war/addons/acz-enhanced-gunplay-mod>).
  It is kept unmodified, for reference and as a fallback unpacker only; it is
  never imported by the mod. Its author did not ship a license statement, so
  **it remains the property of its author, all rights reserved**, and the MIT
  grant below does not apply to it. It is not part of any release archive
  produced by `tools/package_release.sh`. If you redistribute this repository
  and want to be strict, drop that one file (nothing in the build needs it) or
  ask the upstream author for terms.
* `tools/arc/arc_tool.py`, `tools/arc/wpb_dump.py`, `tools/arc/dl.py` — original
  to this project (MIT, below). `arc_tool.py` was written from the decoded
  format; it is read-only and never writes to the game directory.
* `tools/re/*` — original to this project (MIT, below): the RTTI/vtable/xref
  scripts used to produce `docs/RE.md`, `docs/RTTI.md` and friends.
* Everything else (`src/`, `loader/`, `build.sh`, `Makefile`, `ACZPropNav.ini`,
  the `.cmd`/`.ps1` installers, `tools/pnsim`, `tools/*test`, `tools/gen_*`)
  — original to this project (MIT, below).
* No third-party code is linked into the shipped DLLs. The runtime dependencies
  are the Windows system libraries only (`kernel32`, `user32`, `psapi`,
  `advapi32`), linked statically otherwise; the toolchain is mingw-w64.

